Category: IT Services

Location: Fort Western Province Sri Lanka

For an international organization in Spain, we are urgently looking for a REMOTE (Senior) Front-End Drupal Developer. All positions are long-term.

During the corona crisis, interviews will be done through WEBEX, and travel is not required for the interviews.

Tasks and responsibilities

• Assist with the development and maintenance of full-lifecycle implementations of Drupal-based solution;

• Support the website Cybersecurity Project Manager to provide training, layout design, and bulk scripted content migration support for non-compliant websites to Unite Web;

• Undertake a feature gap analysis for each non-compliant websites and Unite Web;

• Develop customized features to help support the migration of each non-compliant websites to Unite Web;

• Provide post-migration support to each non-compliant websites that have migrated to Unite Web;

Profile

• Bachelor or Master degree;

• +2/+5 years of experience in providing assistance to design, development, implementation, and maintenance in developing Drupal 8 web sites is required;

• Experience in development of responsive websites using frameworks (e.g. Bootstrap);

• Proficiency coding in PHP/HTML/CSS/JavaScript and other web development tools;

• Proficiency in using Git for source control management;

• Experience with Agile project development and product delivery;

• Experience with REST API integrations, GIT, MySQL, and MariaDB databases;

• Ability to use wire-frame and modeling tools;

• Knowledge in automated testing, deployment processes, and continuous integration;

Location : Remote;

Salary/Day price : Depending on experience;

